# Stow ignore list for this package (replaces stow's built-in list). Keep it in step with
# the allow-list in dot-claude/.gitignore (the dot-claude-my submodule).
#
# Package root: docs, never stowed.
^/README\.md$
^/\.stow-local-ignore$
#
# Inside ~/.claude: an ALLOW-LIST. Normally stow folds ~/.claude into one link to
# dot-claude/ and these rules never apply. They matter when ~/.claude is a real directory
# (not migrated yet, or recreated by an app). Stow then links the curated files one by
# one and never the runtime state (projects/, sessions/, history.jsonl, the submodule's
# .git file, ...). With --dotfiles, stow matches the translated name (.claude/...).
^/\.claude/(?!(settings\.json|CLAUDE\.md)$)[^/]+$
